      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="lead">I’m Subhasis Jena, a designer and creative technologist based in Bengaluru.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="section-rule" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
      <h2 id="practice-title">How I work</h2>
      <p>My background is in electronics and communication. It shapes the questions I ask when I build an interface. What signal can someone see? What might they miss? What detail would help them decide what to do next?</p>
      <p>I bring those questions to interface engineering and systems diagnostics. In a PyTorch workspace, that can mean putting a shape warning beside the connection that produced it. In a research simulation, it can mean making the local rules visible next to the structure they are meant to form.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
